        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs find on parsed arguments. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A failed parse is returned as a failure. With <computeroutput>--<ref refid="namespacefiles" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">files</ref></computeroutput>, the command lists the files instead of searching them. Without paths, standard input is searched when it is not a terminal. Otherwise the current folder is searched.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>arguments</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The parsed arguments from getArguments. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>input</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The supplied input text, or nullopt for the process standard input.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The exit code, the output text, and the diagnostics. The exit code is 2 when a failure is recorded, except that <ndash/>quiet with a match gives 0. Otherwise it is 0 when a match is found, and 1 when none is found. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
